.TH XCALC 1 "November 2026" "OpenLook"
.SH NAME
xcalc \- OPEN LOOK scientific calculator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xcalc
.RB [ -rpn ]
.RI [ XView-options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The native XView port of X.Org xcalc provides algebraic and reverse Polish
notation (RPN) scientific and programmer calculation. Press F2 or Control-R,
or use the right-click menu, to change mode. Switching modes resets the
calculation and memory registers. The rounded keys are custom drawn in blue,
white and sand tones, with pressed and keyboard-focus feedback.
The supplied calculator icon is used when the window is minimized.
.SH OPERATIONS
Algebraic mode supports operator precedence and parentheses. In RPN mode,
Enter pushes a number onto the four-level stack; Roll rotates the stack
and X:Y exchanges the top two values.
.PP
DRG cycles between degrees, radians and grads. INV changes sine, cosine and
tangent to their inverse functions, log to ten-to-the-power, ln to exponential,
and square root to square. INV followed by DRG converts the displayed angle
to the next unit.
.PP
STO, RCL, SUM and EXC store, recall, add to, and exchange with memory.
In RPN mode, follow STO, RCL or SUM with a register digit from 0 to 9.
EXC exchanges with register zero.
.PP
CE/C clears the entry; pressing it twice in algebraic mode clears pending
operations. AC resets the entire calculator. Backspace edits the current entry.
Invalid domains, division by zero, overflow and exhausted expression stacks
show Error. Clear the error with CE/C or AC before continuing.
.SH PROGRAMMER FUNCTIONS
The base key cycles decimal, hexadecimal and octal (DEC/HEX/OCT).
A through F enter hexadecimal digits. The not, and, or, xor, shl, shr and
mod keys operate on unsigned 32-bit integers. Shifts accept counts from 0 to 31;
left shifts discard bits beyond bit 31. The trunc key removes a fractional part.
Negative, fractional or out-of-range word operands, invalid shifts, and modulus
by zero report Error. Base conversion also requires an unsigned 32-bit integer.
.SH KEYBOARD
Digits, decimal point, +, -, *, /, ^, parentheses and ! enter the corresponding
operations. Return evaluates in algebraic mode or pushes the RPN stack.
Backspace edits; Escape performs AC; Control-Q closes the calculator.
Tab, Shift-Tab and arrow keys move keyboard focus; Space activates that key.
Return always evaluates or pushes the RPN stack. Dragging off a pressed key
and releasing cancels the click.
.PP
Other shortcuts: p for pi, e for Euler's number, E for exponent entry,
s/c/t for sine/cosine/tangent, l for natural logarithm, r for square root,
i for inverse, d for angle units, and n for sign change.
Programmer shortcuts: b for base, % for mod, & for and, | for or, x for xor,
~ for not, and < or > for shifts. Uppercase A-F enter hexadecimal digits;
E selects exponent entry in decimal mode.
.SH NOTES
The calculation engine is derived from X.Org xcalc 1.1.3. Its scientific
display uses eight significant digits for computed decimal results; hexadecimal
and octal words are exact. Xt action resources are not used.
No network connection is needed at build time or runtime.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR olwm (1)
